course: dictionary
lesson: 10258
title: The tonne: a big unit of weight
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tonne is a unit of mass, which is how much something weighs. One tonne is one thousand kilograms, so we use it for very heavy things. «Eagles often use the same nest year after year» and a nest can weigh about 2 tonnes, as much as a car. That is a lot of weight.
explain: To change tonnes to kilograms, multiply by 1,000. To change kilograms to tonnes, divide by 1,000. So 3 tonnes is 3,000 kg, and 4,500 kg is 4.5 tonnes.
explain: In everyday talk, «tonnes of homework» does not mean homework that weighs a tonne. It means a very large amount. Context tells you which meaning is used: «a five-tonne truck» is about weight, but «tonnes of homework» is about a lot.
fact: One tonne is equal to 1,000 kilograms.
fact: «Tonnes» is the plural of tonne, as in «tonnes of sediment».
fact: «The world's rivers carry billions of tonnes of sediment to the sea every year.»
fact: Informally, «a tonne» or «tonnes» can mean a very large amount, as in «tonnes of homework».
exercise: A lorry weighs 3 tonnes. How many kilograms is that? | 30,000 kg | *3,000 kg | 30 kg | 300 kg
exercise: Mia says «I have tonnes of homework» means her bag weighs a tonne. What does it really mean? | Homework is weighed in grams | *She has a very large amount of homework | Her bag weighs exactly one tonne | She has no homework at all
exercise: 4,500 kg is how many tonnes? | *4.5 tonnes | 0.45 tonnes | 450 tonnes | 45 tonnes
test: A whale weighs 5 tonnes. How many kilograms is this? | 50 kg | *5,000 kg | 500 kg | 50,000 kg
test: «The world's rivers carry billions of tonnes of sediment to the sea every year.» What does tonnes measure here? | Time | *Weight, or mass | Temperature | Length
exam: A truck carries 2,500 kg of sand. How many tonnes is that? | *2.5 tonnes | 0.25 tonnes | 25 tonnes | 250 tonnes
